// Expected verdict from J. Ševčík, "Program Transformations in Weak Memory Models", PhD thesis, University of Edinburgh, 2008; checked here under sMRD.
// Load buffering with each location under its own monitor: x under m1, y under
// m2.
//
// Source: Ševčík, "Program Transformations in Weak Memory Models" (PhD thesis,
//         Edinburgh 2008), Figure 1.1B (and Figure 5.1B), "prohibited".
//
// The program is data-race-free, so the DRF guarantee gives it sequential
// consistency: r1 = r2 = 1 is FORBIDDEN, and the only outcomes are r1 = r2 = 0
// and r1 = 1, r2 = 0 -- which are exactly MoRDor's. It needs lock order: before
// it, sMRD treated the locks as no-ops and allowed the outcome.
// Skip/LB+locks.lit is the same shape with one lock.
//
x := 0; y := 0;
{
  lock m1; r1 := x; unlock m1;
  lock m2; y := r1; unlock m2;
} ||| {
  lock m2; r2 := y; unlock m2;
  lock m1; x := 1; unlock m1;
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1) [sMRD]
